nodespot - native radio node and web control panel
===============================================

Open the web UI:      http://<this-host>:8080   (8080 is the default port; see "listen" in nodespot.conf)
Admin account:        sudo nodespot admin create   (shows in the install output as a setup link)
Setup link fallback:  http://<this-host>:<port>/#/setup?code=<code>, with the code from
                      /var/lib/nodespot/setup-code or "journalctl -u nodespot"
Lost password:        sudo nodespot admin reset-password <user>
Accounts:             sudo nodespot admin list
Configuration:        /etc/nodespot/nodespot.conf       (then: sudo systemctl restart nodespot)
Logs:                 journalctl -u nodespot -u nodespot-helper -u nodespot-node

Services
  nodespot.service         the web server, runs as user "nodespot" (hardened, no capabilities)
  nodespot-helper.socket   socket-activated root helper; performs package updates and
  nodespot-helper.service  firewalld changes on request from the web server. It accepts
                        a fixed set of operations only, from root and user "nodespot".

  nodespot-node.service    the native node: one radio (SHARI / SA818 interface), one
                        network mode at a time (AllStarLink, EchoLink or a digital
                        mode). No Asterisk. Runs as user "nodespot-node" with no
                        capabilities. Config: /etc/nodespot/node.json (mode 0600: it
                        holds network passwords) and /etc/nodespot/sa818.json. Control
                        socket: /run/nodespot-node/control.sock (user "nodespot" is a
                        member of group "nodespot-node" to reach it).
                        Logs: journalctl -u nodespot-node

Firewall
  The web port is the one in "listen" in /etc/nodespot/nodespot.conf (default 8080).
  If firewalld is running, installing the package opens it: through the
  firewalld service "nodespot" for 8080, as a plain TCP port for any other port.
  Otherwise open the port yourself if you use another firewall.
  To pick another port (1024-65535, or 80): run the installer again with NODESPOT_PORT (it also opens
  the port in firewalld):
      curl -fsSL https://w1jar.github.io/nodespot/install.sh | sudo NODESPOT_PORT=8181 sh
  or edit "listen" and run  sudo systemctl restart nodespot , then open the port in
  your firewall (firewalld: sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-port=8181/tcp
  && sudo firewall-cmd --reload).
  Port 80 and no other web UI left by an earlier ASL install: run the
  installer with NODESPOT_TAKEOVER=1. It stops and disables Allmon3, the web server of the ASL web UIs (apache2,
  lighttpd or nginx), asl-web-ui and Supermon (those that exist and are on),
  never nodespot-node, records them in /var/lib/nodespot/takeover.list and moves nodespot
  to port 80:
      curl -fsSL https://w1jar.github.io/nodespot/install.sh | sudo NODESPOT_TAKEOVER=1 sh
  Undo (nodespot goes back to its old port, the recorded units are turned on):
      curl -fsSL https://w1jar.github.io/nodespot/install.sh | sudo NODESPOT_TAKEOVER=undo sh

AllStarLink 3 and Asterisk
  Not needed: nodespot runs its own node and never installs them. On a node
  upgraded from 2.x they stay installed; stop Asterisk before the native node
  uses the radio (sudo systemctl disable --now asterisk).

Updates
  Settings > Updates in the web UI (administrators), or the usual:
      sudo apt update && sudo apt install --only-upgrade nodespot
  The repository is added by the install script; see https://w1jar.github.io/nodespot/

Reporting bugs
  Settings > About > Report a bug (prefilled form), and Download diagnostics (admin)
  for a log file with IP addresses and secrets removed. https://github.com/w1jar/nodespot

Removal
  apt remove nodespot   keeps /var/lib/nodespot (users, favorites) and the user
  apt purge nodespot    deletes them, the node config (/etc/nodespot/node.json,
                     /etc/nodespot/sa818.json) and the nodespot-node user, and the state
                     left by 2.x (/var/lib/nodespot-dv, /var/lib/nodespot-config-history,
                     /var/lib/nodespot-dvstate*)

Software AMBE vocoder at install:
  The installer can also install it, with the same code as the Modes page:
      curl -fsSL https://w1jar.github.io/nodespot/install.sh | sudo NODESPOT_VOCODER=1 sh
  If that fails, nodespot stays installed; install the vocoder later from the Modes page.
